\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces AVLips masking intervention at seed\nobreakspace  {}44. Baseline AUC is on clean inputs. $\Delta _\mathrm  {vis}$ is the change after applying full visual masking; $\Delta _\mathrm  {aud}$ is the change after applying full audio masking (both $p=1.0$, masking definition matches Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref {tab:perturbation}). The asymmetric drop under visual masking and neutral response under audio masking that we observed on FAVC FV-RA also appears on AVLips: only \textsc  {TriRoute}\ shows a large $|\Delta _\mathrm  {vis}|$, indicating it is the only model routing predictions through the visual stream on this target dataset as well. Reported at single seed\nobreakspace  {}44 for the perturbation eval (the baseline column in Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref {tab:avlips} is the multi-seed mean).}}{16}{table.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:avlips_perturbation}{{10}{16}{AVLips masking intervention at seed~44. Baseline AUC is on clean inputs. $\Delta _\mathrm {vis}$ is the change after applying full visual masking; $\Delta _\mathrm {aud}$ is the change after applying full audio masking (both $p=1.0$, masking definition matches Table~\ref {tab:perturbation}). The asymmetric drop under visual masking and neutral response under audio masking that we observed on FAVC FV-RA also appears on AVLips: only \method \ shows a large $|\Delta _\mathrm {vis}|$, indicating it is the only model routing predictions through the visual stream on this target dataset as well. Reported at single seed~44 for the perturbation eval (the baseline column in Table~\ref {tab:avlips} is the multi-seed mean)}{table.10}{}}
